          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Do not default into finance simply because you did BCom. It is a genuinely strong fit for many
    commerce graduates, but the strongest specialization decision is the one where you can already
    point to one small piece of real, relevant work — a spreadsheet model, a small campaign, a
    process you improved during an internship — before you even start the MBA. That early proof
    tells you more about fit than the subject name on the specialization brochure.
  </p>

